    {
      "id": "Hstk",
      "code_hash": "75fd49f86437d93594e69d0557ae5d1a",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"objective-function\">Objective Function</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">$$f(\\tilde{\\theta}) = \\frac{\\max_\\delta E[N \\mid \\delta]}{\\mu}</span>\n<ul>\n<li>\\mu \\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\alpha' - \\alpha<sup>*}{\\alpha</sup><em>}\\right)^2\n\\cdot \\mathbf{1}{\\alpha' &gt; \\alpha^</em>}$$</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\beta' \\leq \\beta^*||)</marimo-tex> is guaranteed by the integer bisection.\nOnly <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\alpha'||)</marimo-tex> requires a penalty term.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">If no feasible <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(n||)</marimo-tex> exists, returns a large fixed value (2.0) so the\nGPR learns to avoid such boundary combinations.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
